\details{
Exactly two finite numeric probabilities in \verb{[0,1]} are required, summing to 1
within absolute tolerance \code{1e-6}. Values are never renormalized, rounded,
clipped, complemented, or fabricated. Exact 0, 0.5, and 1 are retained.
Confidence must be a finite numeric scalar in \verb{[0,1]}; missing confidence fails.
Historical generative rows receive \code{NA} decision fields in the normalizer.

The returned choice is authoritative: no argmax substitution is made. If the
alternative exceeds its probability by more than \code{1e-8}, the row fails with
\code{choice_probability_mismatch}. Both probabilities, original selection, and
raw response remain available for later provider/trait/order analysis. Equal
probabilities retain the explicit selection. Mismatches must not be retried
without an explicit future policy. Other failure codes are \code{invalid_choice},
\code{invalid_probabilities}, \code{invalid_confidence}, \code{malformed_decision},
\code{decision_refusal}, and \code{decision_identity_mismatch} (during normalization).
OpenAI's explicit \code{type = "refusal"} is distinct from malformed output. The
current TypeSafe schema has no refusal variant; unknown answer types there
remain malformed rather than being guessed from prose.

Only normalized successful \code{results} are modeling evidence; retained failed
choices are diagnostics. Existing BT/Bayesian/adaptive code is unchanged and
does not consume probabilities as weights, fractional wins, or extra outcomes.
Raw responses may contain sensitive provider content. Do not log them publicly.
